!! Draft ahu → `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-law-of-5s.mem#/rank-consensus`

```text
<<~ ahu #/rank-consensus>>

!! Rank consensus ~ several lenses over one item set

''REACHED ~ the fold.'' Several strict, best-first rankings over the SAME named items may yield one reproducible order. Each ranking names every item exactly once; an absent or repeated item stops the fold rather than inviting a guessed position. A first ranking supplies the stable tie order.

''REACHED ~ two readings.'' Borda adds each item's zero-based positions and advances the lowest sum; a tied sum follows first-ranking order. Kemeny searches the permutations for the order with least total Kendall-tau pair disagreement. Seed that search with Borda, keep the first equal-cost order, and the returned disagreement never exceeds Borda's. Exhaustive search reaches at most eight items; a larger set calls for another method or a refusal, never an unbounded silent search.

''INFERRED ~ the ladder boundary.'' Aperture, action ladder, scope, rating, and stage each name a distinct vocabulary. Their five rows do not themselves rank one shared set of candidates. A caller must first name the common candidates and obtain a strict order over those candidates from each lens it intends to fold. Without that mapping, preserve the separate readings and decline to announce a consensus.

''INFERRED ~ the authority boundary.'' A consensus order compresses disagreement among the supplied readings; it grants no federation rank, gate authority, or world verdict. Keep the input orders and Kendall cost beside the result so another reader can inspect what the fold moved.

<<~/ahu>>
```

Read boundary: no branch received a cherry-pick, merge, stash, or other repository write. The draft rests in this workspace for the controller to place.
